.TH APER-SEARCH 1 "July 28, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper-search \- search a bounded substitution space and render its survivor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-candidate " index" ]
.RB [ \-c " scheme" ]
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.br
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-candidate " index" ]
.BR " " { \-k | \-\-classify }
.br
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.B \--list-candidates
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-l | \-\-list-known }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper-search
exercises the discovery pipeline over deliberately finite square-grid spaces.
The one-type control covers a unit square with half-scale squares.  The
two-type space exhausts all 256 pairs of binary 2 by 2 replacement blocks.
It checks substitution matrices and geometry, verifies several generations,
removes equivalent results under one global square symmetry and type
relabelling, and writes a selected rule or patch as native vector PDF to
standard output.
.PP
The uncoloured geometry remains the periodic square grid.  The semantic tile
types can have nonperiodic symbolic dynamics, but a finite search result alone
does not prove that property.  These are control cases for extending the
search to richer prototiles, not claims of novelty or aperiodicity.
.PP
The known-rule bank contains the Encyclopedia systems independently encoded
by aper.  Classification tests exact canonical rule equivalence only.  Failure
to match this necessarily incomplete bank is not evidence of novelty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \--space " " name
Search
.B square
or
.BR binary-square .
The default is
.BR square .
.TP
.BR \--candidate " " index
Select a zero-based canonical survivor to render or classify.
The default is 0.
.TP
.B \--list-candidates
Write deterministic tab-separated search statistics and every survivor with
its exact executable-bank match, if any.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colour " " scheme
Select
.BR flare ,
.BR grove ,
.BR electric ,
or
.BR tide .
The default is
.BR flare .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Render the patch after 1 through 7 substitutions.
The default is 4.
This option may not be used with rule output.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule
Render the discovered substitution rule instead of a finite patch.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-classify
Write a text classification of the selected survivor against the encoded
known-rule bank instead of rendering PDF.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-known
List the local system id, Encyclopedia record, and source URL for every
encoded known rule.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the control search and render its depth-4 patch:
.PP
.EX
aper-search > square-candidate.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render the rule found by the same search:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --rule > square-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Exhaust the binary square space, inspect its 27 canonical survivors, and
render survivor 22:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --space binary-square --list-candidates
aper-search --space binary-square --candidate 22 > candidate.pdf
aper-search --space binary-square --candidate 22 --rule > candidate-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Inspect the executable bank and classify that survivor:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --list-known
aper-search --space binary-square --candidate 22 --classify
.EE
.PP
Survivor 22 is an exact rediscovery of the encoded two-dimensional Thue-Morse
rule.  Other unmatched survivors remain candidates rather than novelty claims.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.tsv
Metadata-only reference index of the Tilings Encyclopedia substitution pages.
Installed separately by
.BR "make install-encyclopedia" .
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.NOTICE.md
Attribution, licence, and transformation notice for the reference index.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper-search
exits zero after writing the requested PDF, classification, or bank listing.
It exits non-zero if its arguments or candidate index are invalid, the search
invariant fails, or output cannot be written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aper (1)
